},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":26,"finishersRank":16,"finishRateRank":61,"winningTimeRank":18,"winningTimeRankDir":13,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 2003 Comrades Marathon was the 78th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.179 km. The race was held on Monday, 16 June. Conditions: Cool at start with mist in the valleys. Fine and warm later. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nFusi Nhlapo claimed the men's title in 05:28:53, ahead of Oleg KHARITONOV (05:31:42) and Joseph MOLABA (05:31:55). Elena NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:07:47, followed by Olesya NURGALIEVA (06:12:08).\n\nElena NURGALIEVA's 06:07:47 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 13,364 entries, 11,413 runners crossed the finish line (85.4% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,545 men and 1,868 women (16.4% female). The average finish time was 09:56:08.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 672 Silver, 2,436 Bill Rowan, 5,777 Bronze, 2,508 Vic Clapham. 2,286 runners (20.0%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Zeb LUHABE in 12:00:00.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 2001, the field was 12.9% smaller.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 49% of the finishers, with 5,835 seniors (avg 09:42:45) and 5,578 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}